 deciding whether a graph of girth <jats:italic>g<\/jats:italic> in <jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" xlink:href=\"graphic\/jgt21659-math-0004.png\" xlink:title=\"urn:x-wiley:03649024:jgt21659:equation:jgt21659-math-0004\"\/> has a homomorphism to <jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" xlink:href=\"graphic\/jgt21659-math-0005.png\" xlink:title=\"urn:x-wiley:03649024:jgt21659:equation:jgt21659-math-0005\"\/> is NP\u2010complete. We also show that the same dichotomy occurs when considering 3\u2010Colorability or acyclic 3\u2010Colorability of graphs under various notions of density that are related to a question of Havel (On a conjecture of Gr\u00fcnbaum, J Combin Theory Ser B 7 (1969), 184\u2013186) and a conjecture of Steinberg (The state of the three color problem, Quo Vadis, Graph theory?, Ann Discrete Math 55 (1993), 211\u2013248) about the 3\u2010Colorability of sparse planar graphs.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/jgt.21659","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2012,6,27]],"date-time":"2012-06-27T00:40:35Z","timestamp":1340757635000},"page":"85-102","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":19,"title":["A Complexity Dichotomy for the Coloring of Sparse Graphs"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"73","author":[{"given":"Louis","family":"Esperet","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"LABORATOIRE G\u2010SCOP (GRENOBLE\u2010INP, CNRS)  GRENOBLE FRANCE"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Micka\u00ebl","family":"Montassier","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"LaBRI (UNIVERSIT\u00c9 DE BORDEAUX, CNRS)  TALENCE, FRANCE"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Pascal","family":"Ochem","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"LIRMM (UNIVERSIT\u00c9 MONTPELLIER 2, CNRS)  MONTPELLIER, FRANCE"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Alexandre","family":"Pinlou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"n